# NOTE on python3-mcp / python3-pymetasploit3 (0.2.0+pkg8): both were hard
# Depends through pkg7, but NEITHER exists in the Debian archive
# (python3-mcp first enters in sid; pymetasploit3 is Kali-only), so every
# hard Depends made the deb uninstallable on pure Debian. They moved to
# Recommends with a covered fallback: on Kali both apt packages install;
# on Debian the postinst vendor lane pip-installs both (pinned to the
# requirements.txt versions) into /usr/share/daharness/vendor, which
# sitecustomize.py prepends via the existing vendored-wheel lane
# (the pip closure is self-contained; its .so tags match the installing
# interpreter, which on the Debian lane IS the interpreter every deb
# lane runs — 3.13 — so the tag-gate passes; Kali satisfies the bare
# import probe and never reaches the pip lane). If neither lane
# ran (offline Debian install), the gateway still boots: REST lanes stay
# up while /mcp answers an honest 503 and /health reports the lane
# (api_gateway.py fail-soft import).
Recommends: metasploit-framework, zaproxy, python3-mcp,
 python3-pymetasploit3, wordlists,
 jadx, radare2
# Suggests mirrors the framework_doctor probe list (auxiliaries/framework_status.py):
# amass -> auxiliaries/amass.py, ldap-utils (ldapsearch) -> auxiliaries/ldap_search.py,
# exploitdb (searchsploit) -> payloads/searchsploiting.py, ffuf/hydra/sqlmap ->
# payloads/. Every one resolves via shutil.which + $BIN env overrides and degrades
# honestly when absent — optional, so Suggests and never Depends (masscan + the
# engagement-Postgres lane already sit here, plus the deb's own vendored-wheel
# pip lane (python3-pip rides Depends) as the manual Debian recovery path).
Suggests: amass, ldap-utils, exploitdb, ffuf, hydra, sqlmap,
 python3-pg8000, python3-psycopg, python3-yaml,
 masscan, postgresql
Description: headless orchestration harness for authorized security research
 An external LLM (Open WebUI model, gateway or MCP client) semantically
 searches the vector-indexed tool registry (SQLite + numpy) and executes modules
 with result-projection and budget gates. Python orchestrates; a C plugin
 gates Brain event dispatch; systemd runs the system profile (Brain UDS at
 /run/daharness/brain.sock, state at /var/lib/daharness, config at
 /etc/daharness/daharness.env).
 .
 Privileged lanes (raw sockets, low ports) degrade honestly and are
 documented in daharness-safety(7).
 .
 NOTE: the tool registry uses a local SQLite + numpy vector store
 (no server process, no network dependency at build time).
 python3-mcp
 and python3-pymetasploit3 are Recommends with a covered fallback now —
 Kali satisfies both via apt; Debian's postinst pip-installs them into
 the package's own vendor/ tree (sitecustomize-armed). Without either
 lane the gateway's REST API stays up while /mcp degrades honestly
 (see the fail-soft import in api_gateway.py). The Jupyter closure
 (python3-ipykernel + python3-ipython + python3-jupyter-client) stays a
 hard Depends, not the [jupyter] extra: without it
 daharness-kernel.service dies at its lazy import in a
 Restart=on-failure loop (observed 2026-10-20), and Kali rolling builds
 these against the system python (3.14) — the dev pin (6.29.5) predates
 the interpreter the deb lane runs on.